<title>USA: Cantab Pharmaceuticals Q3 full results.</title>
<headline>Cantab Pharmaceuticals Q3 full results.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 mos     3 mos    9 mos    9 mos   9 mos</p>
<p>			 to Sep    to Sep   to Sep   to Sep  to Sep</p>
<p>		30, 1996   30, 1995  30, 1996  30, 1995  30, 1996</p>
<p>			 Unaud-    Unaud-   Unaud-   Unaud-  Unaud-</p>
<p>			  ited	ited     ited     ited  ited(A)</p>
<p>Amounts in accordance</p>
<p>with U.K. and U.S. GAAP:</p>
<p> Revenues	     3,040	 502    3,065	672  $4,781</p>
<p>Operating expenses(B)</p>
<p>		     (2,154)   (1,717)  (6,145)  (5,828)  (9,586)</p>
<p> Operating loss	886   (1,215)  (3,080)  (5,156)  (4,805)</p>
<p>Interest and similar</p>
<p>  income (net)	  504	 178	774	577   1,207</p>
<p> Net profit (loss)  1,390   (1,037)  (2,306)  (4,579) (3,598)</p>
<p>Net profit (loss) per</p>
<p>  ordinary share     0.09    (0.10)   (0.19)   (0.46)  (0.29)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	15,048     9,863   12,207    9,863  12,207</p>
<p>Notes:</p>
<p>(A) U.S. dollar amounts have been translated from or into sterling at the rate on September 30, 1996 of 1.00 pound = $1.56 for information purposes.</p>
<p>(B) Included within operating expenses for 1995 are exceptional costs to date totaling 274,000 pounds which relate to redundancy costs following a strategic review completed in April 1995.</p>
<p>(C) The figures for the financial year ended December 31, 1995 are extracted from the statutory accounts for that year, on which an unqualified report was made by the Auditors, and which have been delivered to the Registrar of Companies for England and Wales.</p>
<p>(D) These financial statements have been prepared in accordance with U.K.</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Cantab Pharmaceuticals plc.</p>
<p>(in thousands of pounds)</p>
